;; Outbound networking denied except to this machine — for a live check whose
;; daemon needs a local model (Ollama on localhost) and clients on 127.0.0.1
;; (the CLI, curl), and nothing else. Not for the app's webview: an app launched
;; under this profile confines the daemon it spawns, but WebKit's Networking
;; process then sets its own block-network flag and the webview's loopback
;; connects fail with EPERM, so the window never reaches its daemon (Q00,
;; 2026-10-12, in every launch checked; plan-rev3 §5.2's launcher (iii), kept
;; for the spawn and daemon-ready only; review C-03). For a GUI check, start
;; the daemon under this profile first, then the app unsandboxed with the same
;; OPENALPACA_HOME_STORE and OPENALPACA_CONFIG_DIR — a Start from inside the
;; app then spawns an unconfined daemon unless §5.2's confined in-app Start is
;; used (review MF-4). Use it from the daemon's FIRST launch:
;; `web_fetch` raises no approval prompt and the shipped research agent has web
;; access, so an unsandboxed daemon reaches the internet whenever a model
;; delegates research (it happened in a live check on 2026-10-03).
;; Usage (macOS; sandbox-exec is deprecated but functional):
;;   sandbox-exec -f scripts/eval/memory/loopback-only.sb openalpacad
;; Prove it before the first model turn: a request to localhost succeeds and a
;; request to a public host fails. `no-network.sb` beside this file is the
;; stricter profile, which also refuses localhost.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network-outbound)
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
